Scan-out: a GPU copy that is still in flight is no longer overwritten by the next frame's copy. Up to two copies are in
flight, into the two buffers that are neither on the panel nor queued for it, and each is shown when it lands. Before,
the next frame's copy went into the in-flight copy's buffer and restarted the wait, so while the GPU stayed busy (the
lock-screen unlock: 74 swaps, 14 on the panel in 2 s) almost no frame reached the panel. coalesced now counts a copy
replaced before its vsync when that happens, not when the next copy is queued.

